1. WeChat, the Linux client of WeChat, was found to have a critical vulnerability

202
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:38,140
Simply enclose the file name with backticks

203
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:40,050
In WeChat, clicking on this file

204
00:07:40,050 --> 00:07:43,020
the characters in the file name will be executed as commands

205
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:46,169
Moreover, any executable commands will be executed.

206
00:07:46,169 --> 00:07:48,669
Currently, WeChat has urgently fixed this vulnerability.

207
00:07:48,669 --> 00:07:52,269
On one hand, the server-side has been configured to block file uploads containing the relevant characters.

208
00:07:52,269 --> 00:07:53,560
cut off the transmission routes

209
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:56,240
On the other hand, the filtering of client-side filenames has been optimized.

210
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:58,320
blocked historical files from triggering the vulnerability

211
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:59,040
2.Windows

